`inline_steps: true` in the manifest embeds every non-detached step's body in its own section and
drops that step's `Run … for content.` fetch line. A detached step keeps fetch form — its agent
fetches its own body.

Twin of `inline-steps-from-the-flag-embeds-non-detached-bodies.txtar`, which plants the same
playbook without the manifest key and passes `--inline-steps`; the two pinned stdouts are
byte-identical.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-inline/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-inline
title: Inline
summary: Bodies embedded in the composed render.
inline_steps: true
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-inline/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  plain: []
  agent: [plain]
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-inline/plain/prompt.md --
---
name: plain
summary: Plain summary.
---

Just do the plain thing directly.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-inline/agent/prompt.md --
---
name: agent
summary: Agent summary.
detached: sonnet:medium
---

Delegated body that must not be embedded.
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-inline
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
Preamble.

